# Round q38bpbug (2026-10-06): Qwen3.8-Flash-Next UD-Q4_K_XL, one stream, after the expert tier's routed rows moved
# from the downs' own stores into the host-mapped page to the tier card's memory and one copy a layer
# (crates/gpu/src/host/tier.rs Parts::enqueue_layer, TierIo::rows). --place bp (A6000 + the 3090 as its expert
# tier, 250 W cap) against --place a (the A6000 alone), same binary, same lease, draft off, prose 512, ctx 4352,
# residency unset (mid-p130-s1 on both plans' load lines).
#
# Cause [measured, functional, not admissible: generate_qwen3moe --place bp, BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1, a temporary
# probe, 63 steps]: the tier's down `_sel` stored each output row as one 4-byte store from lane 0 of its warp, straight
# into the host-mapped page, ~6,400 stores a layer (2.5 tier slots x 2,560 rows). The tier's step graph free-run on the
# 3090 alone over its 48 layers took 13.26 ms (276 us a layer); the same graph with the rows into a device buffer
# 2.04 ms (42.5 us); the go wait, the copies in and the signal 0.70 ms; the wait and signal 0.28 ms. In place, the
# host saw the tier's signal 204 us (p50) after the go, after its own in 2,883 of 3,024 services.
#
# [derived] The step from the host's view of a layer, period = host leg + the tier's lag past the host's signal + the
# card's gap from there to the next go, plus c = 1.70 ms a step outside the layers (fitted to both pre-fix rows:
# a 16.33 ms = 48 x 305.6 us + 1.66; bp 22.25 ms = 48 x 427.5 us + 1.73), from the functional records:
#   a:          leg 79.1 + gap 226.5 (host signal to next go)            = 305.6 us -> 16.37 ms
#   bp before:  leg 39.6 + lag 167.4 + gap 220.5 (tier signal to next go) = 427.5 us -> 22.22 ms
#   bp after:   leg 35.3 + lag  25.8 + gap 225.6                         = 286.7 us -> 15.46 ms
# bp after against a: 16.37 / 15.46 - 1 = +5.9 %. The tier now signals 58 us (p50) after the go, under the A6000's
# shadow (its card leg and shared expert) where its 2.2..2.9 tier slots came off the host's leg; the gap past the
# tier's signal grew 5 us (the shadow now outlasts the tier on some layers). Band +1..+9: the functional rows' window
# scatter (+-3 % a row, the two arms from different runs) and the probe's spin on the host thread.
# Read beside, not judged: GLM-5.3 bp before/after (the lead's sitting) [derived ~0]: its ~1.1 tier slots a row-layer
# x 4,096 rows stored the same way cost ~0.17 ms at ~27 M stores/s [derived from the free runs above], under its 0.47..0.58 ms host
# leg a row-layer (glmbp-ab.card); V4.1's c_two (1.9..2.5 ms a pass over its plan (a) calibration, source open,
# glmbp-ab.card) may hold the same term [not measured].
#
# Resource timeline per bp layer after the fix [derived from the records above]: A6000 front ~194 us, then the wait on
# max(host leg 35, tier 58 from the go, the A6000's shadow ~70), then the join and the next front (the gap, 226); the
# 3090 busy ~55 us of the layer's ~287 (its 2.2..2.9 slots, 2 copies in, one ~100 KB copy out); PCIe ~10 KB in and
# ~100 KB out a layer on the 3090's link, ~25 KB of mapped reads on the A6000's; host DRAM the 0.7 host slots a layer
# (~2 MB); NVMe 0. The wall is the A6000's chain; nothing left on it is the tier's.
#
# Runner (the lead's sitting; the full output to a file first; arms as q38tslots-ab.card's one-stream twins, which the
# runner's --parse-arms took on 2026-10-06; the bare arm is bp, the changed one, so the ratio line's bp / a is
# card.py verdict's changed / base as printed):
#   BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38bpbug-ab.card
#   BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090 BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE=bp BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352 BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off'
#   just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512 prose:512@place=a > <log> 2>&1
# Wall [derived]: 2 arms x 4 rounds, a Qwen3.8 load 25..45 s, the prompt 0.4 s, 96 steps ~1.6 s: 6..9 min.
kind: noninf
question: with the expert tier's routed rows written to the 3090's memory and copied to the page once a layer, does
  one Qwen3.8 stream on A6000 + 3090 (--place bp) decode no slower than on the A6000 alone (--place a)?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96, prose 512, ctx 4352, draft off, residency unset, one stream, A6000 + RTX 3090 (250 W cap) +
  host, --place bp against --place a, same binary, same lease, rounds rotated: (bp - a) / a, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +1..+9
rounds: 4
condition: one runner invocation from a tree holding this round's tier.rs, every arm a fresh load, the order rotated
  each round; the bp arms' load lines name cards=[NVIDIA_RTX_A6000,NVIDIA_GeForce_RTX_3090] with tier=3090 on their
  plan line and the a arms' the A6000 alone; both arms' residency lines read mid-p130-s1 (or the same P); no FAIL row,
  no [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row among the counted rounds; the 3090 at 250 W and no Xid in any witness
  block; the full output to a file first
decide-in: bp is not slower: write the bp and a rows to rig-log's A6000 + 3090 table with the fix's commit, and re-sit
  q38tslots-ab.card's two-stream arms on this binary, whose -24..-6 % band assumed the old tier chain
decide-below: bp still loses or gains under +1 %: one functional BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 run of each arm to re-read the
  gap and the leg (the A6000's shadow, not the tier, now bounds the phase) before any README change
decide-above: bp gains past +9 %: re-derive the gap term, which then fell with the tier's lag (the A6000's join and
  front), before writing the row
#
# Measured 2026-10-09 (the lead's sitting; the log this card's runner names, its witness stamps
# 2026-10-08T15:32Z; one lease, 4 interleaved rounds, prose 512 + 96 tokens, ctx 4352, draft off,
# residency unset — both arms' load lines mid-p130-s1, the witness blocks clean, no
# [cold]/[cpu-busy]/[other-busy] row, no Xid, the 3090 at its 250 W cap):
#   a   61.72 tok/s (step mean 16.20 ms), pp p512 1,033.87
#   bp  63.90 tok/s (step mean 15.65 ms), pp p512 1,427.77
#   decode bp/a 1.0353 +- 0.0081 (paired by round, n 4); pp p512 1.3811 +- 0.0388. The sitting's bp
# plan [derived]: the tier 7,236 experts — the BP_PLAIN/BP_DRAFTED pins at U 4,096 (the load lines'
# ubatch=4096; crate model's qwen4exp metas), the census's free bytes and the ctx 4352 moving it
# within a few (the residency rule's P 130 = half the plan's fewest stage experts a layer, 260
# against the pin's 261). The release tapes read beside, not this card's conditions (MTP on, ctx
# 8192): the code tape's decode 107 against 96.0, its prefill 1,274 against 922.
#
# Break-even for the census rule: the Qwen3.8 family's unset --place picks bp only when the bp plan's
# tier holds at least E* experts, E* = 1,152 [derived] (24 a layer on the 48 card-routable layers).
# The gain's terms per layer, from the functional fit above with the tier's count t swept — the ids
# the tier takes come off the host's set (the A6000 keeps plan (a)'s row; both cards plan to their
# own budgets):
# - the host leg falls with its ids: 79.1 -> 35.3 us a layer as the host's ids fell 250 -> 99 at the
#   sitting's tier, 0.2905 us a layer an expert [derived, the two fitted legs];
# - the tier's leg: its signal 58 us after the go at 150.75 a layer = 44.8 us fixed (the copies in,
#   the launches into its rows, the rows' copy out, the signal) + 0.0874 us an expert [derived: 10
#   routed slots a layer (n_used) uniform over the 512 ids, an expert 3.13 MB at 700 GB/s]; it sits
#   under the host's leg past t 90.7, and past it a layer-period hands 0.0808 us an expert back;
# - the gap (the A6000's join and next front) 226.5 us under both arms; bp's step cost outside the
#   layers +70 us over a's (the fit's c, 1.73 against 1.66 ms).
# The fit at the sitting's tier reads +6.2 % where the lease measured +3.4 % (the functional rows
# run hot: the probe's spin on the host thread), so the model is scaled to the lease's 552 us a step
# at 7,236 [derived] and the sitting's ruler (same-binary paired ratio, +-0.81 % at n 4) held across
# the sweep. Lower bound over the grid: -0.82 % at 384 (8 a layer; the mean itself ~0 there — bp's
# fixed costs unpaid, the mean crossing 0 at 392), -0.61 at 576 (12), -0.19 at 960 (20), -0.03 at
# 1,104 (23), +0.03 at 1,152 (24), +0.45 at 1,536 (32), +2.15 at 3,072 (64), +3.52 at 4,352 (90, the
# sweep's peak — past it the tier's leg outlasts the host's and hands back), +2.60 at the sitting's
# 7,236. The crossing is 1,126 [derived]; E* the first whole count a layer past it. The prompt side
# reads the same host-id term (its host union at P 512 fell 6.59 -> 3.39 ms a layer-batch, q38tier's
# functional rows): +4.7 % at E* against its own +-3.9 % band, its lower bound crossing at ~985
# [derived] — under the decode's, whose fixed cost the fit separates; a sitting that needs the
# prompt periphery re-derives both. A sitting whose lower bound reads below this band's re-derives
# E* from the measured gain before the rule moves.
